Source: bank.inc
     1 				; Extended RAM (130XE): the $4000-$7FFF window shows one of four 16 KB banks.
     2 				;   bank 0, 1  cell records, 64 rows each, one 256 byte page per row, 16 records of 16 bytes
     3 				;   bank 2     string pool index table (2 bytes per pool string, up to 8192)
     4 				;   bank 3     string heap (len byte + Latin-1 text), append only
     5 				; All code that opens the window lives outside $4000-$7FFF. PORTB bits 2,3 pick the bank, bit 4 = 0 lets the CPU see it,
     6 				; bit 7 stays 1 (0 would map the self-test ROM at $5000), bit 0 keeps the OS ROM (floating point package) on.
