Source: fpu.inc
     1 				; Number helpers on the 6 byte BCD (OS floating point) format: BV holds a number.
     2 				;   byte 0 = sign<<7 | (exponent + 64), exponent in base 100; bytes 1-5 = ten BCD digits (first pair is the integer pair).
     3 				; rounding and formatting work on the digits directly (exact); the OS ROM does the arithmetic.
     4
     5 				; BV digits -> DG[1..10] (DG[0] = 0, room for a carry)
